brotli: no model("small") attribute on LoongArch.

brotli 1.2.0 marks its static tables with __attribute__((model("small")))
whenever the compiler knows the `model` attribute. Clang knows it only on
LoongArch, where the valid code models are normal, medium and extreme, so
every file including common/constants.h fails with
  error: code model 'small' is not supported on this target
Skip the attribute there, as on every target that does not have it.

--- a/c/common/platform.h
+++ b/c/common/platform.h
@@ -665,7 +665,10 @@
 #undef BROTLI_TEST
 #endif
 
-#if BROTLI_GNUC_HAS_ATTRIBUTE(model, 3, 0, 3)
+/* The only `model` value used here is "small", which is an ia64 code model. On
+   LoongArch - the other target that knows the attribute - it is rejected: the
+   code models there are normal, medium and extreme. */
+#if BROTLI_GNUC_HAS_ATTRIBUTE(model, 3, 0, 3) && !defined(__loongarch__)
 #define BROTLI_MODEL(M) __attribute__((model(M)))
 #else
 #define BROTLI_MODEL(M) /* M */
